"id":"euler.lemma-2.6","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma 2.6","locator":"Lemma 2.6, Section 2","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma 2.6.** Assume (2.7), and let $\\mathbf a$ be the amplitude vector with $\\mathbf a(t_0)=-E_1(t_0)/S+E_2(t_0)$, that is, with $(\\alpha_1,\\alpha_2)(0)=(-1,1)$ in (2.3), the initial data of the reference solution. Then $\\alpha_2>0$ on $0\\le\\tau\\le T$, and $$\\begin{equation}\n \\left|\\frac{\\alpha_1}{\\alpha_2}+Y\\right|\\le CT^C\\delta,\\qquad\n \\alpha_2\\le|\\mathbf a|\\le(1+CT^C\\delta)\\alpha_2. \\tag{2.17}\n\\end{equation}$$ Moreover, $$\\begin{equation}\n \\left|\\log\\frac{|\\mathbf a|}{a_{\\rm ref}}\\right|\\le\\varepsilon. \\tag{2.18}\n\\end{equation}$$ For $0\\le\\tau_1\\le\\tau_2\\le T$, let $\\Phi(\\tau_2,\\tau_1)$ map $\\mathbf b(\\tau_1)$ to $\\mathbf b(\\tau_2)$ for every amplitude vector $\\mathbf b$. It maps the plane perpendicular to $k(\\tau_1)$ onto the plane perpendicular to $k(\\tau_2)$, and $$\\|\\Phi(\\tau_2,\\tau_1)\\|\n \\le CS\\,\\frac{|\\mathbf a(\\tau_2)|}{|\\mathbf a(\\tau_1)|}.$$","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-2.6","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-2.6","id":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.6%22%2C%22euler.lemma-2.4%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.6%22%2C%22euler.lemma-2.4%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-2.4"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-2.6","id":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed